QUESTION: Convert Quarter rows into columns and calculate total sales for each Year and Quarter. Display 'NA' when sales are NULL.

Input:

Plain Text
Year Quarter Sales
2020 Q1 90
2020 Q1 10
2020 Q2 70
2020 Q3 130
2020 Q3 20
2020 Q4 NULL
2021 Q1 40
2021 Q2 NULL
2021 Q3 120
2021 Q4 20
 

Required Output:

Plain Text
Year Q1 Q2 Q3 Q4
2020 100 70 150 NA
2021 40 NA 120 20

ANSWER:

SQL
SELECT
Year,
 
COALESCE(
CAST(SUM(CASE WHEN Quarter = 'Q1' THEN Sales END) AS VARCHAR(20)),
'NA'
) AS Q1,
 
COALESCE(
CAST(SUM(CASE WHEN Quarter = 'Q2' THEN Sales END) AS VARCHAR(20)),
'NA'
) AS Q2,
 
COALESCE(
CAST(SUM(CASE WHEN Quarter = 'Q3' THEN Sales END) AS VARCHAR(20)),
'NA'
) AS Q3,
 
COALESCE(
CAST(SUM(CASE WHEN Quarter = 'Q4' THEN Sales END) AS VARCHAR(20)),
'NA'
) AS Q4
 
FROM Sales
GROUP BY Year
ORDER BY Year;

Question: Write an alternative query for FULL OUTER JOIN

SELECT *
FROM A
FULL OUTER JOIN B
ON A.X = B.Y;


Answer: Using LEFT JOIN, RIGHT JOIN and UNION



SELECT *
FROM A
LEFT JOIN B
ON A.X = B.Y
 
UNION
 
SELECT *
FROM A
RIGHT JOIN B
ON A.X = B.Y;

UNION removes the duplicate matching rows, giving the equivalent FULL OUTER JOIN result.

